  "summary": "PercentField now takes its decimal-place width from `scale` instead of `precision`, read ONCE and shared by the readonly `toFixed` face, the number input's `step` attribute and the slider's step, guarded with `typeof` because `scale: 0` is a valid declaration. A `decimal(10, 2)` percent field renders `25.00%` and steps by `0.01` instead of rendering `25.0000000000%` and stepping by `1e-10`. An absent `scale` keeps this widget's own 2, so the repair is invisible to a percent field declaring neither member; the whole-percent convention detected from `max > 1` is untouched. No exported type, prop or symbol changes (the widget reads its field bag through a cast), so `Clause-2: no` holds. Card assignee was `os-sales` (set by PM) and untouched; the newest `Claim:` comment 5725884752 names THIS branch and THIS session. The issue body shows NO sanitizer truncation - it ends with its attribution footer and all three fenced blocks plus the dedup-word line are intact.",
  "premise_checks": {
    "zone2_1_defect_sites": "CONFIRMED, line numbers included, on base 1b969aec6 (the brief's 0ee6e31 had moved; re-read as instructed). `const precision = percentField?.precision ?? 2;` at :14, the readonly `toFixed(precision)` at :35, `const sliderStep = Math.pow(10, -precision)` at :126, the input `step={Math.pow(10, -precision).toFixed(precision)}` at :140 and the slider `step={sliderStep}` at :155 - all five still present and still with the stated effect.",
    "zone2_2_counter_precedent_4361": "READ AT SOURCE (body + both comments) and it is NOT a fork - but the card's stated REASON is half wrong and must not be reused. objectui#4361's ruling point 2 says an explicitly authored `precision` WINS, and `CurrencyField` resolves it in the widget itself (`currencyField?.precision ?? currencyFractionDigits(currency)`), so it is a direct read of the field member, not merely 'a parameter name for a width the caller already resolved' as the card states. What still makes it no precedent here: its competing source is a currency's ISO 4217 minor-unit count and never `scale`; a currency field's face carries no decimal-place member `precision` could be confused with; and that card deliberately escalated the contract question upstream (objectstack#7918) rather than settling what an authored `precision` means. It rules nothing about percent and nothing about `scale`.",
    "zone2_3_scale_reaches_widget": "CONFIRMED at four independent points rather than assumed: (a) `FieldSchema` in `@objectstack/spec` declares `scale` on the flat field face for every field type, with the verbatim 'Decimal places (non-negative integer)'; (b) the metadata-admin designer offers the control under the predicate `type in ['number','currency','percent']` (pinned in `predicate.test.ts`); (c) `@objectstack/objectql`'s record validator enforces `scale` by REJECTION (`max_scale`) on the branch that includes `t === 'percent'`; (d) both detail hosts that build the inline-edit field bag - `RecordDetailPanel` and `RelatedList` - already forward `scale` beside `precision`, and `InlineFieldInput` hands that bag straight to `PercentField`. CAVEAT, filed as finding 1: `@object-ui/types`' `PercentFieldMetadata` declares `precision` and NOT `scale`, which is why those hosts cast.",
    "zone2_4_sibling_reach": "CONFIRMED. PR objectui#9566 merged 2026-09-15T16:47:37Z with 12 files: `.changeset/9295-percent-surfaces-read-scale.md`, three `PercentCellRenderer*` pins, `packages/fields/src/index.tsx`, `packages/plugin-detail/src/DetailView.tsx`, three `summaryChip.*` pins, two `useColumnSummary.*` pins and `packages/plugin-grid/src/useColumnSummary.ts`. No widget file, so `PercentField.tsx` is untouched by it - the premise of the whole card holds."
  },
  "decisions": {
    "readonly_face": "Takes `scale`; absent `scale` keeps this widget's own 2. Rule applied: move the MEMBER that is read and nothing else, so the repair is invisible to a field declaring neither member (pinned as a MUST-NOT-CHANGE control). Choosing 0 instead (agreeing with `PercentCellRenderer`) would change behaviour for every percent field in the tree that declares nothing - a bigger user-visible move than the defect, on no contract basis, and ruling 4 makes agreement neither goal nor premise.",
    "step": "Takes the SAME single `scale` read with the same absent default, so the input's `step` attribute and the slider step stay tied to the displayed width. Reason stated rather than inherited: a control whose step is finer than its displayed width offers a value it then rounds away, and the widget's own pre-existing comment already tied slider granularity to the input.",
    "guard": "`typeof declaredScale === 'number'`, not `??`. The dispatch's Zone 3 note said a `?? 2` default reintroduces the `scale: 0` bug; MEASURED, it does not - `0 ?? 2` is `0`, so only `||` drops a declared zero. `typeof` was chosen for a different reason: it also refuses a `scale: \"2\"` arriving from JSON metadata, and it is the guard `NumberField` and this widget's own `max` read already use.",
    "no_type_widening": "`PercentFieldMetadata` was NOT widened to declare `scale`, although it arguably should (finding 1). The widget reads `field as any`, so the fix compiles and works without it; widening an exported type would void this card's `Clause-2: no` per ruling 3, and `packages/types` is outside the declared file surface."
  },
