  "gate_derivation": "`scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs` refuses to answer for objectui by design, so the list was derived from this repo's own `package.json` scripts and `.github/workflows/` against what the diff really touches. Deliberately NOT run, with reasons: `pnpm lint` / `pnpm test` / `pnpm type-check` whole-farm turbo runs (CI owns them; the affected package's own script was run in full instead), `pnpm check` (builds the CLI, nothing in the diff reaches it), `check:handler-key-reads` (covers `on*` handler keys only - measured from its own header, `scale` is not in its population), `check:vi-mock-*` (the new test declares no `vi.mock`), `check:i18n-*` (no locale strings moved), `test:dist` (pins `@object-ui/components` artifacts). Exit codes were captured with `cmd > log 2>&1; EXIT=$?` in every case - never across a pipe.",
  "tests": "NEW: `packages/fields/src/__tests__/PercentField.scale-9568.test.tsx`, 7 cases, every one through the component and reading the DOM it produced - the readonly span's text and the `step` attribute the browser's spinner obeys - plus one driven keystroke for the slider, whose step is a prop rather than an attribute. REVERSE VERIFICATION (fix committed first, then the pre-fix file put back on disk): mutation proved by object hash (on-disk 8f3636857 == base blob, != HEAD blob 2706ad136) and by anchor counts (`percentField?.precision ?? 2` back to 1, `declaredScale` 0, `Math.pow(10, -scale)` 0); vitest exit 1 with 6 failed / 1 passed. The single pass is the MUST-NOT-CHANGE control, which is the point of it. Measured failure texts: '25.0000000000%' where '25.00%' expected; step '0.0000000001' where '0.01' expected; slider ArrowRight emitting 0.250000000001 where 0.2501 expected; '25.00%' where '25%' expected for `scale: 0`. RESTORE proved by hash equality to the HEAD blob and an empty `git diff HEAD`, from a `trap ... EXIT INT TERM` with absolute paths. Typecheck coverage of the new test was verified rather than assumed: `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json --listFiles` lists both the test file and the widget.",
