  "deviations": [
    "Base commit: the brief's `0ee6e31` had moved; the worktree was cut from `origin/main` at `1b969aec6` and `origin/main` was merged once before the PR (bringing `6a0d1a435`, a scripts-only change), giving head `2e421f19`. The three differential gates and the new pin were re-run on that merged head.",
    "eslint narrowing, declared: `pnpm lint` is `turbo run lint` over every package and belongs to CI. What ran here is `@object-ui/fields`' own `lint` script IN FULL (249 files by eslint's own `--format json` count, both changed files in the population), so nothing inside the affected package was excluded. No config in this repo enables type-aware linting (no `parserOptions.project` / `projectService`), so this diff cannot move a verdict on a file it does not touch.",
    "Commit trailers use the repo's own model-free spelling (`Co-authored-by: Claude` with the noreply anthropic address - angle brackets deliberately not written here, because GitHub's body sanitizer eats tag-shaped fragments - plus `Claude-Session:`), which is what the last six commits on `main` carry and what the dispatch contract requires, rather than the model-named spelling the harness reminder offered.",
    "No label write: the dispatch's write budget named only the PR and this comment, and objectui applies path labels from its own `labeler.yml` workflow. `needs:contract-review` is a seat's to hang or not; it is neither hung nor removed here, and PR 9804 currently carries no labels.",
